  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7ed8d592803d6492b8f1f0ac1555a1ea, type: 3}
  m_Name: Telemetry
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: InsightsSamples.Common::InsightsSamples.Common.SampleInfo
  id: 13-telemetry
  number: 13
  title: Telemetry
  series: Behaviour data
  icon: activity
  scenario: Weld along a seam
  realWorld: "Welding trainees practice running a bead along a seam. Instructors care about technique, the torch's travel angle and its distance from the seam over time, not just the finished weld, so the app samples both several times a second while the learner welds."
  teaches: TrackObject, Telemetry
  sceneName: Telemetry
  appWidePrefab: {fileID: 0}
  whatThisShows: Telemetry is for continuous measurements. Abxr.Telemetry sends your
    own at a steady rate while they matter; a TrackObject component samples an object's
    position on its own.
  tryThis:
  - Hold the button on the torch and drag it along the seam, from one yellow mark
    to the other.
  - 'Weld again and wander off the seam: the weld fails, and distance_to_seam_mm
    shows why.'
  watchFor:
  - One live torch_technique row, updating five times a second while you weld.
  - weld_torch Position from TrackObject, once per Telemetry Tracking Period (10
    s by default) while the torch moves and turns.
  lessonScript: TelemetrySample.cs
  lessonScriptLine: 34
  dashboardNotes:
  - methodPrefix: Telemetry
    note: 'Telemetry: measurements over time, per session'
  expectedOnPass:
  - method: Telemetry
    name: torch_technique
    count: 1
    atLeast: 1
    status: 
  expectedOnFail:
  - method: Telemetry
    name: torch_technique
    count: 1
    atLeast: 1
    status: 
